<title>SWITZERLAND: SNB leaves Swiss discount rate unchanged.</title>
<headline>SNB leaves Swiss discount rate unchanged.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Swiss National Bank (SNB) said it left its discount rate unchanged at 1.0 percent after a regular weekly meeting of the three-member policy-setting board.</p>
<p>&quot;Nothing was changed,&quot; an SNB spokesman said in answer to an enquiry after today's meeting.</p>
<p>No rate change had been expected on financial markets. The SNB last lowered the disocunt rate to 1.0 percent from 1.5 percent on September 26.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Newsroom, +41-1-631 7340</p>
